590	  // Deploy-funnel COMPLETION — hosting's authoritative, server-side bottom of the
591	  // funnel, the counterpart to placeOrder / placeGameOrder. Hosting does NOT flow
592	  // through the shared Stripe fulfilment bus (lib/fulfil-checkout.ts has no hosting
593	  // kind — a $0 first month captures a card in `mode:"setup"`, and the charge is the
594	  // wallet debit inside orderHostingAccount), so THIS is its shared success path.
595	  // Recorded here (not on the idempotent-replay early return above) so a retry never
596	  // double-counts. Replaces the client-side trackDeployComplete removed from
597	  // HostingDeployWizard, keeping all three products on one authoritative userId-keyed
598	  // completion. Best-effort + double-guarded so it can never disturb the placed order.
599	  try {
600	    await recordDeployFunnelComplete({ product: "hosting", step: "Complete", stepIndex: 7, userId: user.id });
601	  } catch {
602	    /* never let funnel bookkeeping affect a completed order */
603	  }
604	
605	  // Server-side Meta CAPI `Subscribe` — the free-month hosting signup is a browser-
606	  // ONLY conversion otherwise (HostingDeployWizard fires nxTrack('hosting') client-
607	  // side), so an ad blocker / privacy browser silently drops it and the campaign
608	  // never learns the signup happened. Firing it here too — with the SAME event_id
609	  // the browser pixel uses (idempotencyKey) — means Meta dedupes the two into ONE
